.env
.runtime.env
*.log

# Compose auto-loads this if present — a local escape hatch (e.g. for the
# postgres-init bind-mount workaround the README documents), never meant
# to be committed.
docker-compose.override.yml

# Builds edp-migrate from this repo's own local source (see README.md) —
# only usable here, in the private core-tool repo, never in the public
# poc-environment mirror. Gitignored, not just left out of the sync
# workflow, so it can never end up in that mirror's history in the first
# place — recreate it locally from README.md's own copy if it goes
# missing.
docker-compose.dev.yml

# up.sh/seed.sh's own state — not something a fresh clone should start with.
.seed-state/
